      "title": "Aaple Sarkar Portal to Remain Closed Until October 21, 2026! Know the Reason and Which Services May Be Affected",
      "summary": "The Maharashtra Government’s Aaple Sarkar portal and certain other online government services are reportedly scheduled to remain temporarily unavailable from 4:00 PM on October 16, 2026, until October 21, 2026. According to a report published by ABP Majha, the downtime is due to a software upgrade from Version 1 to Version 2.0. During this period, citizens may face difficulties applying for government certificates, submitting online applications, and accessing other related services. Citizens are advised to check the official portal for updates on service restoration.",
      "body": "Aaple Sarkar Portal Temporarily Closed in Maharashtra\n\nThere is an important update for citizens across Maharashtra. The Aaple Sarkar portal, which provides access to various Maharashtra Government online services, is reportedly scheduled for a temporary shutdown due to technical maintenance and a software upgrade.\n\nAccording to a report published by ABP Majha, the services will be unavailable from 4:00 PM on October 16, 2026, until October 21, 2026.\n\n1. Why Is the Aaple Sarkar Portal Closed?\n\nAccording to the report, the portal’s software is being upgraded from Version 1 to Version 2.0. The purpose of this upgrade is to improve the system, address technical issues, and make online government services more convenient for citizens.\n\n2. Which Services May Be Affected?\n\nDuring the scheduled downtime, citizens may experience difficulties accessing services available through the Aaple Sarkar portal, including:\n\nApplying online for government certificates.\n\nSubmitting applications for various government services.\n\nAccessing application-related services and completing online transactions.\n\nChecking or managing certain service requests.\n\nThe exact impact may vary depending on the service and the systems undergoing maintenance.\n\n3. When Will the Portal Start Working Again?\n\nAccording to the news report, the services are expected to remain unavailable until October 21, 2026. Citizens should check the official Aaple Sarkar website for confirmation that the portal has resumed normal operations, as the actual restoration time may depend on the completion of the technical work.\n\n4. What Should Citizens Do?\n\nCitizens who need to apply for certificates or complete other government-related work should plan accordingly. If a service is unavailable, check the portal again later rather than repeatedly attempting to submit the same application. Follow official announcements for updates on the restoration of services.\n\nImportant Note\n\nThe report concerns a temporary service shutdown, not the permanent closure of the Aaple Sarkar portal. The information and expected dates are based on the published news report; users should verify the latest status through the official website.",
