      "title": "Government Hostel Admission 2026–27: Professional Course Application Deadline Extended to 10 October",
      "summary": "The application deadline for Government Hostel admission for professional courses has been extended to 10 October 2026. The deadlines for the second round of Classes 11–12 and non-professional courses, and for Swadhar renewal applications, remain 30 September 2026.",
      "body": "According to the HMAS notice shared, students applying for Government Hostel admission for professional courses for the academic year 2026–27 can apply during the extended period from 1 October to 10 October 2026.\nStudents with New + Approved or Renew + Approved applications in 2025–26 can apply as Existing Applicants. Students newly admitted to professional courses in 2026–27 can apply as New Applicants.\nThe second-round application deadline for Classes 11–12 and non-professional courses is 30 September 2026, with no extension.\nThe Swadhar Scheme renewal deadline is also 30 September 2026. Students who do not renew within the prescribed period will be treated as unwilling to receive the benefit, and their applications will be declared ineligible. Students facing technical difficulties should contact the concerned Assistant Commissioner, Social Welfare office before the deadline.",
